-- title:
--   Bounded left Λ_w-stable subgroups of a local division quaternion algebra are principal
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\Lambda\subseteq\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is a maximal order in the sense of the project: it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, it is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$, and any submodule with these four properties containing it equals it. Let $w$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ and write $B_w=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$ for the tensor product with the adic completion, and $\Lambda_w=$ [`Submodule.localBox`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) $\Lambda\,w$ for the additive subgroup of $B_w$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb{Q}_w$. Assume every non-zero element of $B_w$ is a unit, let $p$ be a prime with $p\in w$, and let $M\subseteq B_w$ be an additive subgroup which contains a non-zero element, satisfies $dx\in M$ for all $d\in\Lambda_w$ and $x\in M$, and is bounded in the sense that $p^{n}M\subseteq\Lambda_w$ for some $n\in\mathbb{N}$. Then there is $x_0\in M$ which is a unit of $B_w$ such that for every $x\in B_w$ one has $x\in M$ if and only if $x=dx_0$ for some $d\in\Lambda_w$, i.e. $M=\Lambda_w x_0$.
--
--   This is the principality of bounded left $\Lambda_w$-stable subgroups (fractional left ideals) of a local quaternion division algebra, the structural input needed to compare local orders. It is used in [`QuaternionAlgebra.localBox_eq_localBox_of_forall_iff_mem_range_of_isMaximalOrder_of_mem_asIdeal`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.localBox_eq_localBox_of_forall_iff_mem_range_of_isMaximalOrder_of_mem_asIdeal), on the Čerednik–Drinfeld side of the argument.
